  "final_report": "I'll start by locating the project files.The bug is clear: `total -= price` subtracts instead of adding.**Bug found and fixed.**\n\nIn `prices.py`, `sum_prices` accumulated the total with `total -= price` (subtraction) instead of addition, so any input produced the negated sum (e.g. `[2, 3, 7]` → `-12`).\n\n**Change made** (only `prices.py`):\n```python\ndef sum_prices(prices):\n    total = 0\n    for price in prices:\n        total += price\n    return total\n```\n\n**Verification result (actual):** I ran `python.exe verify.py` with the specified interpreter. It exited with code 0 and printed `Verification passed` on stdout (stderr empty). So all three assertions in `verify.py` (`sum_prices([2, 3, 7]) == 12`, `sum_prices([]) == 0`, `sum_prices([-1, 4]) == 3`) now hold.\n\nNote: `notes.txt` also mentions `sum_prices` but is not implementation code, so I left it untouched.",
  "source_after": "def sum_prices(prices):\n    total = 0\n    for price in prices:\n        total += price\n    return total\n"
